{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>In place of every firstborn.</b> The firstborn were not entitled to an inheritance, so that they would have no occupation other than the service of HaKadosh Baruch Hu, and would be zealous and trained in it. And once the Levites were taken in their place, HaKadosh Baruch Hu commanded that no inheritance be given to the Levites either — but the tithes are given to them. Therefore the firstborn takes a double portion: his own portion, which is his due, and the portion due to the Levite."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:16:20.763515165Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}